The McGurk effect is a phenomenon where the perception of what is heard can be influenced by what is seen [1][2][4]. In an illusion, a video where an audio stream of a language token $x$ is visually dubbed over by a person saying $x^{ ackprime}
e x$ affects a listener if they perceive what is being said to be $y
e x$ when watching the illusory video, but perceive $x$ if they had either listened to the audio stream without watching the video or had watched the original unaltered video [1][2][3].

